# Rank 1025 / CVE-2024-29857: importing an EC certificate with crafted F2m
# parameters burns CPU in Bouncy Castle. The binary-field curve degree m comes
# from the certificate and drives the field arithmetic, and nothing limited it,
# so a large m makes curve evaluation run far longer than any real key requires
# (CWE-400, with CWE-125 also assigned). The fix 56daa6eac5 caps it:
#
#   int maxM = ImplGetInteger("Org.BouncyCastle.EC.F2m_MaxSize", 1142); // 2 * 571
#   if (m > maxM)
#       throw new ArgumentException("F2m m value out of range");
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost, measured. The weakness class is real, an untrusted
# numeric dimension driving superlinear work with no ceiling, but the check the
# fix adds cannot be demanded generically. Counting parameters of that shape in
# this library, methods and constructors taking an integer dimension such as m,
# n, size, len, bits or degree, gives 243 in the elliptic-curve and math
# namespace and 336 across crypto/src. Exactly one of them, the F2m degree,
# needed the ceiling this CVE added, so a rule requiring an upper bound on such
# parameters would report on the order of 336 sites for one true positive in
# the very library the CVE was filed against.
#
# The judgement is also not structural. Knowing that the degree drives
# superlinear field arithmetic, and that 1142 is the sane ceiling because the
# largest standard binary curve is 571 bits, is cryptographic domain knowledge
# rather than anything the shape of the code carries. An allocation-oriented
# concept does not fit either: code.LengthDerivedAllocation (VYQL-DOS-006)
# describes a parsed length controlling an allocation, while here the cost is
# computation time and nothing is allocated from m.
#
# Current behaviour on the real file is unchanged by the patch: both revisions
# report the same four VYQL-NUM-005 rows and one VYQL-CFG-014 row, none of which
# concern the degree, so there is no focused evidence either side.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1025: binary-field curve accepts an unbounded degree from the caller"
  lang csharp
  file crypto/src/math/ec/ECCurve.cs
  reject VYQL-DOS-006
  code
  ```
  public abstract class AbstractF2mCurve : ECCurve
  {
      public static BigInteger Inverse(int m, int[] ks, BigInteger x)
      {
          return new LongArray(x).ModInverse(m, ks).ToBigInteger();
      }

      protected AbstractF2mCurve(int m, int k1, int k2, int k3)
          : base(BuildField(m, k1, k2, k3))
      {
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1025: fix rejects a degree above the configured maximum"
  lang csharp
  file crypto/src/math/ec/ECCurve.cs
  reject VYQL-DOS-006
  code
  ```
  public abstract class AbstractF2mCurve : ECCurve
  {
      public static BigInteger Inverse(int m, int[] ks, BigInteger x)
      {
          int maxM = ImplGetInteger("Org.BouncyCastle.EC.F2m_MaxSize", 1142);
          if (m > maxM)
              throw new ArgumentException("F2m m value out of range");

          return new LongArray(x).ModInverse(m, ks).ToBigInteger();
      }

      protected AbstractF2mCurve(int m, int k1, int k2, int k3)
          : base(BuildField(m, k1, k2, k3))
      {
      }
  }
  ```
